# ce-firstboot-tweaks — webOS CE: (a) point the default-wallpaper entries in
# the customization payload's customization.json at a CE wallpaper before the
# customization service runs them; (b) once per flash, drop stale /media/cryptofs copies of
# apps this image bakes into the rootfs (cryptofs survives Doctor flashes and
# a stale copy shadows the baked app).
#
# (a) must stay EARLY and has no cryptofs dependency — the customization
# service reads that file on this same boot. (b) writes to cryptofs, which
# is mounted ~100s before it accepts writes on a fresh flash: this job fires
# on `stopped configurator`, which happens inside that window (seen live on
# 600011: flag written at 18:29, cryptofs not writable until ~18:30). Every
# rm would then fail silently and the flag would be set anyway, leaving a
# previous install's Preware/Govnah/core-app copies shadowing the baked ones
# forever — and with a no-reboot OOBE there is no second boot to repair it.
# So (b) waits for a real write, verifies each removal, and only flags when
# the store is clean. See ce-cryptofs-seed for the same pattern.

start on stopped configurator
start on first-use-finished

console none

script
    exec sh -e /usr/palm/ce-seed/jobs/ce-firstboot-tweaks.sh
end script
